# Position sources for the cruise tracklines: bin/build_cruise_tracks.py
# reads this file when its openvdm.yaml hook passes
# --position-sources=/opt/openvdm/server/etc/cruise_position_sources.yaml.
# The installer copies it from its .dist; edit the copy to match this ship.
# These match the sample data (OceanDataTools/openvdm_sample_data).
#
# CollectionSystem (optional): the collection system transfer these sources
#   belong to. The script fails if its hook names another one; without it,
#   they apply to whichever the hook names.
# PositionSources: one entry per trackline, each with:
#   device: the name in the trackline files' names
#           (<cruiseID>_<device>_Trackline.json and .kml)
#   type:   the data dashboard data type of its position files, the
#           data_type its plugin gives them (openrvdas_plugin.py here)
#   extent: true (optional, one source at most): the source the cruise's
#           bounding box comes from; without it, the first
CollectionSystem: OpenRVDAS
PositionSources:
  - device: POSMV
    type: gga
